                <strong>Chzzk does not support separate server-side VOD mute tracks:</strong>
                <p>
                  Unlike Twitch's legacy Track 6 VOD mute feature, Chzzk encodes live stream audio (Track 1) directly into its VOD replay.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Additionally, Chzzk VOD replays are not stored indefinitely; retention periods depend on streamer tier and view counts (Rookie 30 days/conditional 7 days, Pro 60 days/conditional 14 days, unpublished 2 days). Please refer to <a href="#ch4-vod-retention" style="color: var(--doc-cyan); text-decoration: underline;">Official Chzzk VOD Retention Policy</a> for full details.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Therefore, the primary reason streamers separate OBS audio tracks is <strong>local multi-track recording for YouTube video editing and permanent archiving</strong>.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

